  "test": "Read the 7-segment code first (also shown on the thermostat). Thermistors: unplug the harness and ohm per pins, compare with the chart. Transducers: measure VDC plugged in (pin 1-3 = 5 V, pin 2-3 vs chart). Reset: cycle R power.",
  "notes": "Pin pair 4-3 (black sleeve) = outdoor ambient RT13 in every source. The manuals disagree about pins 6-5 and 2-1: the terminal table, the sensor-operation text, the E416 text and Figure (Temperature Sensor Specification) each put the coil/liquid sensor and the 10K resistor(s) in different places. Trace the brown-sleeve wires before condemning anything on 6-5 or 2-1; a fixed resistor reads about 10K ohms at any temperature, a sensor changes with temperature. EL19KPV: Table 6 (p.40) says COIL and DIS are 10K resistors; E416 says resistor on 5-6; Figure 46 (p.78) shows coil 6-5 brown and \"discharge N/A\" on 2-1. Replacement outdoor control kit: 508718-01 (EL18KCV/EL19KPV).",
  "gaps": [
   "6-pin harness conflict",
   "Refrigerant detection sensor wiring not mapped",
   "Inverter codes not mapped"
  ],
