  "test": "Status: amber LED, 2-digit code = short flashes then long flashes. Continuous off = check 115 V at L1/L2 and 24 V at SEC-1/SEC-2; continuous on = 24 V present; rapid flash = polarity reversed. Code recall: R lead off, reset power, SW1-1 ON. Component test: R lead off, reset power, SW1-6 ON - inducer on for the whole test, igniter and blower 15 s each; 11 = no errors, 25 = setup error.",
  "notes": "Same board and plug numbering in 58SP0A-01SI (diagram A190274) and -02SI (A210176, label 344740-201 rev E). PL1-3 is drawn to the board edge with no device (HPS input on the two-stage board). Codes: 11, 12, 13 limit lockout, 14 ignition lockout, 21 gas heating lockout, 22 abnormal flame, 23 pressure switch did not open, 24 fuse, 25 model/setup error, 31 pressure switch did not close or reopened, 33 limit circuit fault, 34 ignition proving failure, 45 control circuitry lockout.",
