  "notes": "UC board LEDs (green / yellow / red): yellow 1 flash = low side fault / low pressure trip (red on = LPCO lockout after 3 trips); yellow 2 = high side fault / HPCO trip (red on = HPCO lockout); yellow 4 = locked rotor; yellow 5 = open circuit (no compressor current >4 h); yellow 7 = open run circuit (red on = lockout); yellow 8 = low or high line voltage; yellow 9 = low pilot voltage (<18 VAC secondary); yellow + red on = compressor protector open. No EEV, no pressure transducers.",
