  "notes": "Red LED: steady = internal fault; 1 = flame with no call; 2 = pressure switch stuck closed/inducer error; 3 = 1st stage pressure switch stuck open/inducer error; 4 = open limit; 5 = open rollout or fuse; 6 = pressure switch cycle lockout; 7 = lockout retries; 8 = lockout recycles; 9 = grounding or reversed polarity; 10 = gas flow with no call; 11 = limit open - blower failure; 12 = igniter relay failure; 3 double = 2nd stage pressure switch stuck open; rapid = twinning error. Amber: 1 = low heat call, 2 = high heat call, 3 = W2 without W1, 4 = Y without G, rapid = low flame sense. Green: steady = standby, rapid = fan call, 1 = low cool, 2 = high cool. No thermistors. Same 12-pin pin numbers on Rev AA (0140F02011-A), AB (0140F02058-A) and AC (0140F02347-A) diagrams.",
